prompt.template:
You are adding parameter validation to enforce the Express.js error handling pattern.

Target file: {{target_file}}
Findings: Load from /tmp/validation-findings.json

For each finding:
1. Add parameter validation at the start of the function
2. Use appropriate error types:
   - TypeError for type mismatches
   - RangeError for bounds violations
3. Include descriptive error messages with actual values:
   - Use JSON.stringify() for parameter values
   - Format: "Invalid {param}: expected {type}, got ${JSON.stringify(value)}"

Example pattern:
```javascript
function status(code) {
  if (!Number.isInteger(code)) {
    throw new TypeError(`Invalid status code: ${JSON.stringify(code)} - must be integer`);
  }
  if (code < 100 || code > 999) {
    throw new RangeError(`Invalid status code: ${JSON.stringify(code)} - must be between 100-999`);
  }
  // ... rest of function
}
```

Modify {{target_file}} to add validation to ALL functions in the findings.
